This directory is vendored from choudoufu
(https://github.com/INTENTIUS/choudoufu), internal/live/azsweep, at commit
9807fdc1fa595e6d425cc541e8d43d48f43dde6e (branch integration/choudoufu-engine).

Every .go file here is covered by the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0,
file by file, as its own header says (SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0). The
MPL text is at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. The rest of this repository is
Apache-2.0; MPL-2.0 is file-level, so the two sit side by side and nothing
outside this directory takes on the MPL.

Files carried unchanged: attrs.go, doc.go, errors.go.

Files modified for plunge (each stays MPL-2.0):

  credentials.go  builds the credential with azidentity (client secret when
                  the arguments name one, otherwise DefaultAzureCredential)
                  in place of OpenTofu's azurerm backend auth package, which
                  plunge does not carry; metadata_host is refused, and the
                  cloud comes from the azcore presets by name.
  client.go       reads the marker key from plunge's markers package
                  (markers.TagStack) in place of choudoufu's tofu-estate.
  tags.go,        use a plain http.Client in place of OpenTofu's
  keyvault.go     internal/httpclient.
  plunge.go       new: the marker key binding above, and Credential and
                  Scope exported for plunge's ARM lister.

Not carried: every _test.go file.
